| B. Czech, Y. Feng, X. Wu, M. Xie, *Fun with Graph States: Nonlocal Bell pairs and the Arf Invariant*, arXiv:2606.06582v2, §2.1 Eq. (11), §4.1 Eq. (40), §5.1, Appendix B (Eqs. (130)–(131)) and §B.2 | Closest prior work. `literature-attested`: for any graph $G$ on $M$ vertices with adjacency matrix $A$, $\langle+|^{\otimes M}|G\rangle$ is zero or equals $(-1)^\Delta2^{-\operatorname{rank}_{\mathbb F_2}A/2}$ with $\Delta$ the Arf invariant of the quadratic refinement $x^{\mathsf T}A^{\mathrm{upper}}x$ (Eqs. (11), (40)); since $Z_n^{(\mathtt q)}$ (Eqs. (130)–(131), same normalisation as Convention 2.2) is an inner product of two graph states on $Nn^{\mathtt q-1}$ qubits, this gives a general $\mathbb F_2$-rank-and-Arf method for $Z_n^{(\mathtt q)}$ of graph states at every $n$ and $\mathtt q$, and §5.1 gives a second, cycle-based formula for expectation values of permutations. §B.1 computes the multi-invariants of the three-qubit chain; §B.2 computes $S_n^{(4)}$ of the four-qubit path graph with one qubit per party at $n=2,3,4$ (ranks $18,76,198$, $\Delta=0$; $S_3^{(4)}=\tfrac{19}{9}\log2$; the rank $76$ at $n=3$ agrees with $\sum_{t\ne0}\rho_t=76$ from Theorem 3.1), and states $S_n^{(4)}=(2+n^{-2})\log2$ for all $n$ only conditionally on an unpublished polynomiality result. The source does not contain: the reduction of that rank to the ranks $\rho_t$ of $N\times N$ matrices over $\mathbb F_2(\zeta)$ and the positivity of $Z_n^{(\mathtt q)}$ for all odd $n$ and all $\mathtt q$ (Theorem 3.1); the masked-rank identity for characters with at most three values and the partition decomposition for $\mathtt q\ge4$ (Proposition 4.1, Corollary 4.2); or the failure of the masked-rank expression (Proposition 5.1). 